    compassExplainerCta: 'What are needs?',
    compassExplainerWhat:
      'A need is what you fundamentally require to feel safe, connected, or alive — like closeness, rest, or orientation. That\'s different from a want: a want is usually one particular way of meeting a need (e.g. "that one phone call"), while the need behind it is broader (e.g. connection). Two people with the same need can have very different wants for meeting it.',
    compassExplainerWhyHaveTitle: 'Why do we have needs at all?',
    compassExplainerWhyHave:
      'Needs are essentially built-in signals — similar to hunger or thirst, just for emotional and social things instead of food. They indicate what matters for your wellbeing right now, even when that signal is sometimes quiet or hard to interpret.',
