    compassExplainerWhy:
      "Needs often point to what actually matters right now — even when that's hard to notice in the moment itself. Naming a need makes it more concrete: a vague \"something's off\" becomes a clearer \"I think I need some rest right now\" — and that's easier to act on than a vague unease.",
