    systemMapHint: "An overview of the app's red thread as a path you can explore.",
    nameExplanationTitle: 'Why "von mir aus"?',
    nameExplanationText: '"Von mir aus" carries two meanings in one German phrase: starting from me — and: if I want to. Both belong together.\n\nThe first step here always comes from you, not from a requirement or a schedule. That is self-efficacy in a small way: sensing for yourself what is called for right now, instead of waiting for someone else to decide what is good for you.\n\nIn trauma work, loss of control is often a central experience — things happened without being asked. This app deliberately reverses that: nothing happens here without you having started it. Only offers you can accept — or not.\n\nAnd sometimes it is simply that: a quiet permission to yourself to keep going, starting from right here.',
