    threeStatesSource: 'This description is based on a polyvagal-informed view. As noted above: that the nervous system has different activation states is well established — the exact role of individual vagal branches is a scientifically debated model, not a fully proven mechanism.',
    ladderTitle: 'The polyvagal ladder',
    ladderIntro: 'A helpful image: the three states like rungs of a ladder, from the top (connected) to the bottom (withdrawn).',
    ladderDownNote: '↓ Under stress, the nervous system can move down the ladder, rung by rung.',
    ladderUpNote: '↑ The way back up is just as possible — through the same rungs, not in one jump.',
